title: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> merges with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>!
subtitle: A behemoth of the Commonwealth Right is formed...
view-if: year >= 1931 and (100 - unionist_relation) >= marcher_votes and unionist_ideology == "Right" and (unionist_leader == "Sedgewick" or unionist_leader == "Aldermoor") and (((in_marcher_majority or in_left_front) and (not marcher_heartland or in_left_front_heartland or in_marcher_majority_heartland)) or (marcher_votes + pro_republic + left_strength >= 150)) and traditionalist_leader == "Trevannon" and stegerwald_transformation_timer == 0 and not concord_formed and not dkp_merger_waiting
max-visits: 1
tags: event
priority: 3
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/dvpcampaign.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
new-page: true

= The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> merges with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>

The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, having undergone a major transformation into a center-right <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span> under [+ unionist_leader +], has been flirting with the idea of merging with [+ traditionalist_leader +]'s <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> for the past few months. [? if marcher_votes + pro_republic < 120 or ((in_marcher_majority or in_left_front) and (not marcher_heartland or in_left_front_heartland or in_marcher_majority_heartland)): Their mutual opposition in the current governing coalition, newfound ideological closeness, and shared fears of both the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>—coupled with their electoral decline at the hands of the former—have pushed them toward closer cooperation. ?][? if marcher_votes + pro_republic >= 120 and not ((in_marcher_majority or in_left_front) and (not marcher_heartland or in_left_front_heartland or in_marcher_majority_heartland)): Their growing ideological alignment, shared commitment to the Republic, and mutual anxiety over the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>—whose monumental electoral gains threaten to overturn the Commonwealth’s conservative order—have pushed them toward closer cooperation. ?]

We have suffered a falling out with the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, which now seeks to sever its remaining ties to us in order to clear the path for a merger with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. Our few remaining allies within their ranks have been sidelined—left powerless to obstruct the party’s rightward drift. This shift has enabled the party’s leadership, alongside newly integrated right-wing dissenting politicians, to open negotiations with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> on a possible unification. 

However, resistance remains: the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>’s old guard, led by figures like Westmore and Tilford, remain deeply skeptical of the merger, citing fundamental disagreements over key "national questions," such as War Loans.

- @cvp_dnvp: Negotiations between the two parties have begun.

@cvp_dnvp
on-arrival: {!
Q.concord_traditionalist_balance = 50;

if (Q.unionist_relation >= 20) {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= 10;
} else {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 10;
}
if (Q.peoples_party) Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 5;
if (Q.left_split) Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 5;
if (Q.sapd_formed) Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 5;
if (Q.reformist_strength >= Q.left_strength + Q.center_strength) {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 5;
} else if (Q.left_strength >= Q.reformist_strength) {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= 10;
}
if (Q.royalist_votes >= 35) {
  Q.concord_traditionalist_balance = Q.concord_traditionalist_balance + ((50 - Q.concord_traditionalist_balance) * 0.6);
} else if (Q.royalist_votes >= 30) {
  Q.concord_traditionalist_balance = Q.concord_traditionalist_balance + ((50 - Q.concord_traditionalist_balance) * 0.4);
} else if (Q.royalist_votes >= 25) {
  Q.concord_traditionalist_balance = Q.concord_traditionalist_balance + ((50 - Q.concord_traditionalist_balance) * 0.2);
}
if (Q.pro_republic >= 70) {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 20;
} else if (Q.pro_republic >= 55) {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 10;
} else {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= 20;
}
if (Q.nationalism < 45) {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 10;
} else if (Q.nationalism < 55) {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= 10;
} else {
    Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= 20;
}

Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= (Q.marcher_votes / 4);

if (Q.bruning_coalition_dissent < 1) Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 10;
if (Q.war_loans <= -2) Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += 15;

Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= Q.bruning_coalition_dissent*10;
Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= Q.traditionalist_angry*5;

Q.concord_traditionalist_balance += (Q.unionist_votes - Q.bvp_votes)*2;
Q.concord_traditionalist_balance -= (Q.traditionalist_votes)*2;

!}
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

A great deal of concessions are required to bring both sides to a comprehensive agreement, as both parties go through their differences and attempt to design a uniform policy if they were to merge. However, it is likely one party will have the upper hand in negotiations, either due to their electoral advantage, or reluctance forcing more sweeping concessions to be granted.

Pro-merger factions:

<span style="color: #000000;">Far-Right</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>)

<span style="color: #000000;">Labor Right</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>)

<span style="color: #000000;">dissenting Right</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>)

<span style="color: #6D5298;">Faithful Socials</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>)

<span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>)

Skeptical factions:

<span style="color: #000000;">the Unionists</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>)

<span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservatives</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>)

Opposed factions:

<span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>)

<span style="color: #385A38;">Agrarians</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>)

Balance of Power: [+ concord_traditionalist_balance : concord_traditionalist_balance +]

@cvp_dnvp_menu


- @monarchy
- @war_loans
- @economy
- @coalition
- @congress

@war_loans
title: The "National Questions".
subtitle: The debate over the Commonwealth's lost lands, the fulfillment of War Loans, rearmament, and more.
view-if: not concord_reparations
on-arrival: concord_reparations = 1
go-to: reparations_right if concord_traditionalist_balance < 45; reparations_moderate if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 45 and concord_traditionalist_balance < 55; reparations_left if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 55

The War Loans issue remains the most contentious point of contention between the two parties, with starkly opposing views on how to handle the Commonwealth’s financial obligations. The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, including Trevannon himself, staunchly opposed the Serannus Plan and has previously clashed with the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> over foreign policy achievements such as the Vera Accords in the past.

@reparations_right
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance += 10; concord_right += 5; nationalism += 10; pro_republic -= 5; west_relation -= 1; east_relation -= 2; unionist_relation -= 5; guild_unionist += 4; guild_dnf -= 4; burgher_unionist -= 4; burgher_gold += 4; burgher_lvp += 4; landed_dnf -= 2; landed_unionist += 2
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> have used their leverage to edit in their most important goals to the party program.

War Loans - the Commonwealth must push for the complete abolition of War Loans and the revocation of the National-Debt Clause, but will continue payments in the meantime

The Eastern Policy - the Commonwealth should seek to pressure the Allied States for the return of our former lands, force if necessary later down the line

The Western Policy - Closer ties between the Freehold and the Commonwealth, push for accession of the Freehold, referendum for the contested border marches

The Commonwealth Army - Continue the secret rearmament and refitting of the army

@reparations_moderate
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> have begrudgingly come to an agreement, as pragmatism wins the day; the Commonwealth can't simply refuse to pay.

War Loans - the Commonwealth should seek a policy of fulfillment, hoping for a revision of the Etaluxia treaty

The Eastern Policy - the Commonwealth should seek to pressure the Allied States for the return of our former lands, peacefully later down the line

The Western Policy - Closer ties between the Freehold and the Commonwealth, referendum for the contested border marches

The Commonwealth Army - Continue the secret rearmament and refitting of the army

@reparations_left
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance -= 10; concord_left += 5; nationalism -= 10; pro_republic += 5; west_relation += 1; east_relation += 1; unionist_relation += 5; guild_unionist -= 8; guild_dnf += 8; landed_unionist -= 4; landed_dnf += 4; burgher_unionist += 6; burgher_gold -= 2; burgher_ddp -= 2; burgher_lvp -= 4; burgher_marcher -= 2
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> have used their influence to push for a more restrained and diplomatic foreign policy, aligning with the legacy of Stratton.

War Loans - the Commonwealth should be develop closer ties with the West, hoping for a revision of the Etaluxia treaty

The Eastern Policy - the Commonwealth should seek to peacefully settle disputes in the East

The Western Policy - Closer ties between the Freehold and the Commonwealth

The Commonwealth Army - Continue the secret rearmament, but scale it down

@monarchy
title: The Commonwealth Monarchy
subtitle: The debate over whether the party should be a <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> or a <span style="color: #808080;">monarchist</span> one.
view-if: not concord_monarchy and concord_reparations
on-arrival: concord_monarchy = 1
go-to: monarchy_right if concord_traditionalist_balance < 45; monarchy_moderate if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 45 and concord_traditionalist_balance < 55; monarchy_left if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 55

The issue of the Commonwealth <span style="color: #808080;">monarchy</span> remains highly divisive, with both parties holding starkly different views. Despite the unfeasibility of a restoration in the current political climate, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> has never ceased advocating for a return to the days of the old Empire. The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, on the other hand, has consistently been a staunch <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> force since the birth of the Unity Republic. Perhaps the influence of the <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> will outweigh the strong objections from the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s old guard.

@monarchy_right
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance -= 10; concord_right += 4; unionist_relation -= 5; pro_republic -= 5; landed_unionist += 4; landed_dnf -= 2; landed_other -= 2; guild_unionist += 6; guild_dnf -= 4; guild_other -= 2; burgher_unionist += 2; burgher_dnf -= 2; commons_unionist -= 5; commons_marcher += 3; commons_ddp += 3; commons_lvp += 3; disfavored_unionist -= 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; disfavored_ddp += 2; disfavored_lvp += 2; faithful_unionist -= 4; faithful_marcher += 4; faithful_ddp += 2; faithful_lvp += 2
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span> have successfully pushed for the inclusion of support for a constitutional monarchy in the party platform. However, it is no longer a central pillar of the party's ideology.

Monarchy - Support for a constitutional monarchy, similar to the stance of the[? if not gold_exist or lvp_formed:&nbsp;former?] <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>.

Democracy - Favoring a strengthened presidency, while maintaining a pro-democratic stance

@monarchy_moderate
on-arrival: concord_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; guild_dnf += 4; landed_dnf += 2; guild_unionist -= 4; landed_unionist -= 2; commons_unionist -= 2; commons_marcher += 2; commons_ddp += 1; commons_lvp += 1
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span> have leveraged their influence to block an outright endorsement of <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">blica</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">nism</span> in the party platform, ensuring their views remain represented despite being a vocal minority.

Monarchy - No official party position on monarchism.

Democracy - Supports a presidential government, otherwise maintain the status quo

@monarchy_left
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance += 10; concord_left += 4; unionist_relation += 15; pro_republic += 15; landed_unionist -= 6; landed_dnf += 4; landed_other += 2; guild_unionist -= 6; guild_dnf += 4; guild_other += 2; burgher_unionist -= 4; burgher_dnf += 2; burgher_other += 2; commons_unionist += 5; commons_marcher -= 3; disfavored_unionist += 4; disfavored_marcher -= 3
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span> attempted to insert their long-standing support for monarchism into the party platform, but were decisively outvoted by the staunchly <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, along with support from some <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span>.

Monarchy – Official endorsement of the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> system

Democracy – Favors a more parliamentary system, with presidential decrees as a last resort

@economy
title: Economic Policy
subtitle: The debate over agriculture, welfare, and the calamity.
view-if: not concord_economy and concord_reparations and concord_monarchy
on-arrival: concord_economy = 1
go-to: economy_right if concord_traditionalist_balance < 30; economy_moderate if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 30 and concord_traditionalist_balance < 40; economy_left if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 40

A potential big-tent <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span> faces the difficult task of addressing the diverse economic concerns of its broad electoral base. This base spans across farmers, aristocrats, landowners, large businesses, small businesses, civil servants, white-collar workers, blue-collar urban workers, and many others from all walks of life.

@economy_right
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance += 10; concord_right += 5; landed_unionist += 2; landed_dnf -= 2; guild_unionist += 6; guild_dnf -= 2; guild_gold -= 2; guild_lvp -= 2; burgher_unionist += 4; burgher_dnf -= 2; commons_unionist -= 3; commons_marcher += 5; disfavored_unionist -= 3; disfavored_marcher += 5
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span> have used their leverage to edit in their economic beliefs into the party program.

Taxation - Avoid tax increases at all costs, especially on businesses

Welfare - the Commonwealth cannot afford welfare and maintain a balanced budget at the same time, one has to go

Labor - Strongly against any <span style="color: #c00000;">socialistic</span> policies that benefit the Free Guilds

Economic calamity - Maintain fiscal orthodoxy, productive industries and agriculture must be kept afloat though

@economy_moderate
on-arrival: guild_unionist += 4; guild_gold -= 2; guild_lvp -= 2; burgher_unionist += 4; burgher_dnf -= 2; commons_unionist -= 1.5; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_unionist -= 1.5; disfavored_marcher += 3; concord_economy_keynes = 1
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> have begrudgingly come to an agreement, as pragmatism wins the day. The party must represent its diverse base, for the national community.

Taxation - Avoid tax increases at all costs

Welfare - Focus on funding the current system, as the poor are suffering

Labor - Against any <span style="color: #c00000;">socialistic</span> policies, but neutrality in labor affairs is a key component of the national community.

Economic calamity - Experiment with a public works plan, combined with an increase in the money supply

@economy_left
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance -= 10; concord_left += 5; landed_unionist -= 4; landed_dnf += 2; landed_gold += 2; landed_lvp += 2; guild_unionist -= 6; guild_dnf += 2; guild_gold += 4; guild_lvp += 4; burgher_unionist += 4; burgher_dnf -= 2; burgher_ddp -= 2; commons_unionist += 8; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_unionist += 8; disfavored_marcher -= 5; disfavored_royalist -= 3; concord_economy_keynes = 1
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> and <span style="color: #6D5298;">Faithful Socials</span> have used their influence to advocate for a pro-worker and more ambitious economic policy, recognizing that workers are a key part of the national community.

Taxation - Implement more progressive taxes and regulations, to ensure a fair Commonwealth

Economic Policy - Implement a 'Social market economy', a middle way between capitalism and <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span>

Economic calamity - A public works program is needed, the people must get back to work

@coalition
title: Inter-Party Relations
subtitle: The debate over whether we should be considered as a coalition partner.
view-if: concord_reparations and concord_economy and concord_monarchy and not concord_coalition
on-arrival: concord_coalition = 1
go-to: coalition_right if concord_traditionalist_balance < 65; coalition_moderate if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 65 and concord_traditionalist_balance < 75; coalition_left if concord_traditionalist_balance >= 75

The integration of the staunchly anti-<span style="color: #9B0000;">Vaelist</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> into the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> will likely rule out any future cooperation with them. However, a vocal minority of progressives still exists within the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, who may argue in our favor.

@coalition_right
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance += 10; concord_right += 5; unionist_relation -= 10; landed_unionist += 6; landed_dnf -= 2; landed_other -= 2; landed_royalist -= 2; guild_unionist += 10; guild_dnf -= 4; guild_gold -= 2; guild_lvp -= 2; guild_other -= 4; burgher_unionist += 6; burgher_dnf -= 2; burgher_other -= 4; commons_unionist -= 3; commons_marcher += 3; commons_ddp += 2; commons_lvp += 2; disfavored_unionist -= 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; disfavored_ddp += 2; disfavored_lvp += 2; concord_coalition_right = 1
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span> have used their leverage to edit in their vehement anti-<span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> stance into the party platform.

<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> - Strongly against governing with

<span style="color: #FFCC00;">**Liberals**</span> - Preferred governing partner

<span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> - Strongly against governing with

<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> - Suspiciously ambiguous

@coalition_moderate
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 5; landed_unionist += 4; landed_other -= 2; landed_royalist -= 2; guild_unionist += 6; guild_gold -= 2; guild_lvp -= 2; guild_other -= 4; burgher_unionist += 2; burgher_other -= 2; concord_coalition_moderate = 1
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span> have used their leverage to edit in their vehement anti-<span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> stance into the party platform. However, the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> has managed to keep an open door for future cooperation—though it's not a very wide one.

<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> - Against governing with

<span style="color: #FFCC00;">**Liberals**</span> - Preferred governing partner

<span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> - Strongly against governing with

<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> - Suspiciously ambiguous

@coalition_left
on-arrival: concord_traditionalist_balance -= 10; concord_left += 5; unionist_relation += 15; landed_unionist -= 4; landed_dnf += 2; landed_other += 4; guild_unionist -= 6; guild_dnf += 2; guild_other += 4; burgher_unionist -= 4; burgher_other += 4; commons_unionist += 3; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_unionist += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; concord_coalition_left = 1
go-to: cvp_dnvp_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span> have attempted to use their leverage to edit in their vehement anti-<span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> stance into the party platform. However, the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> and [+ unionist_leader +] has managed to keep an open door for future cooperation.

<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> - Open to an agreement

<span style="color: #FFCC00;">**Liberals**</span> - Preferred governing partner

<span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> - Strongly against governing with

<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> - Against governing with


@congress
title: With all differences resolved, the <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span> is formed! 
view-if: concord_reparations and concord_economy and concord_coalition and concord_monarchy
on-arrival: {!
Q.concord_gold_trigger = 0;
if (Q.gold_exist && Q.gold_votes < 5 && !Q.lvp_formed && !Q.lvp_merger_2_timer && !Q.lvp_timer_2_trigger) Q.concord_gold_trigger = 1;
if (Q.marcher_heartland && !Q.in_marcher_majority_heartland && !Q.in_left_front_heartland) Q.heartland_coalition_trigger = 1;
if (Q.in_weimar_coalition && !Q.in_social_liberal_coalition || Q.in_grand_coalition || Q.in_popular_front) Q.federal_coalition_trigger = Q.time;
!}
face-image: img/cvp.jpg
call: cvp_formed
achievement: christliche_volkspartei

The agreement is finalized, and the <i>Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</i> (<span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span>) is born.

The <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span> aims to follow the Ashford Program of 4285, transforming the Commonwealth Right into a party that rallies around <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>, <span style="color: #586593;">democratic</span>, <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth</span>, and <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> principles.

- @cvp_party_congress_go
- @cvp_dvp_merger

@cvp_party_congress_go
title: First <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> Congress
subtitle: The future of this new party will be decided here.
view-if: not concord_gold_trigger
go-to: cvp_party_congress

@cvp_dvp_merger
title: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> also wish to join.
subtitle: An unexpected third suitor.
call: cvp_dvp_formed
view-if: concord_gold_trigger

Before the <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span> was to be announced to the public, representatives from the beleaguered <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> have shown their interest in joining the arrangement as well.

This leaves the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> as the only liberal party in the political landscape, now flourishing with defections from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s left wing.

- @cvp_party_congress
